course: dictionary
lesson: 8111
title: Renters and rent
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A renter is someone who pays money to use something that belongs to someone else. Most often that is a home. «Renting means paying a landlord every month to live in a home that belongs to someone else.» The clues are paying, every month, and belongs to someone else, so a renter pays regularly for a place they do not own.
explain: Now look at «Renters usually pay a deposit at the start and sign an agreement.» A deposit is money paid at the start, and signing an agreement means making a promise. Put the clues together and a renter is someone who has agreed to live in a home without buying it.
explain: The word can also mean someone who hires something for a short time, such as a car. The word stays the same, but the thing rented changes. Check the sentence: does it talk about a home, or about something used for a short time? That tells you which meaning is used.
fact: A renter is a person who pays money to use something that belongs to someone else.
fact: «Renters» pay rent to a landlord, usually every month.
fact: A landlord is the person who owns the home that a renter lives in.
fact: «Renters» usually pay a deposit at the start, and it comes back if the home is left in good condition.
fact: A renter can also be someone who hires a car or other item for a short time.
exercise: «Renting means paying a landlord every month to live in a home that belongs to someone else.» What is a renter? | A person who builds houses | A person who sells cars | A person who owns the home they live in | *A person who pays money to live in a home that belongs to someone else
exercise: «Renters usually pay a deposit at the start and sign an agreement.» Find and copy the word that tells you when the deposit is paid. | *start | agreement | renters | usually
exercise: Maya hires a bike for one hour at the seaside. What is she, in this sense? | *A renter, because she hires something for a short time | A homeowner who has bought the bike | A builder who fixes bikes | A landlord who owns the bike
test: «Renters sign a tenancy and pay a deposit that comes back if the home is left in good condition.» What must happen for the deposit to come back? | The renter buys the home | The landlord sells the home | *The home is left in good condition | The renter pays more rent
test: «Renters' rights» and «rising rents» are in the news. Which word tells you that rent can go up? | Agreement | Deposit | *Rising | Landlord
exam: Which of these is a renter? | A girl who owns the flat she lives in | A girl who builds flats for other people | A girl who sells her house to buy a bigger one | *A girl who pays a landlord each month to live in a flat she does not own
